<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The SplashScreen API's "animated icon" stage, deliberately blank (#141).

     The platform draws this masked to a circle at icon scale on top of
     windowSplashScreenBackground. Painting it the SAME brand dark as that
     background makes the stage a flat field, so the boot reads as:

         flat #07071a  ->  full-bleed ace pilot (@drawable/splash)
                       ->  the same pilot, moving (BootSplash.tsx)  ->  table

     Before this, the stage showed @mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground — the ace
     pilot again, but round-masked at icon scale — which made him jump scale
     twice on the way in. He cannot be crop-matched to a full-bleed still at
     icon size, so the honest fix is to not show him here. The LAUNCHER icon is
     untouched; this drawable is only ever the splash stage.

     It doubles as the cover for the brief dark gap between the native splash
     handing off and the WebView's first paint: same colour, so nothing flashes. -->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="@color/spaceBg" />
</shape>
